<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Layout xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS COMMENT SITS INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT DELIBERATELY. A comment placed ABOVE <Layout>
        breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with a misleading "unable to find matching parent
        xml file" error.

        Buyer__c and Materials_Released_Date__c ADDED 2026-08-20 (Workstream D6.1, buyer activity
        timeline, disposition-tranche-2-requirements.md §3). Both fields are reachable
        elsewhere as of this change, but not from a page layout, which is the exact stub-layout
        defect this repo hit this week on BOV_Submission__c and Disposition_Offer__c (see those
        layouts' own headers) - a field that exists in the schema and is granted FLS but has no
        rendered input is functionally invisible to an analyst.

        🔴 NDA__c HAS ONLY ONE LAYOUT, SHARED BY BOTH Acquisition_NDA AND Disposition_NDA RECORD
        TYPES. There is no per-record-type layout separation on this object today (confirmed:
        objects/NDA__c/layouts holds no second file, and no layoutAssignments entry scopes a
        second one). So both new fields are layout-reachable on EITHER record type once this
        deploys - they are NOT hidden from an acquisition NDA the way this file's own
        instructions asked for a permission-set-level exclusion. FLS is the actual gate: neither
        field is granted on DPEG_Acquisition_Edit / DPEG_Acquisition_View / DPEG_Admin_Access
        (see the field files and the two disposition permission sets), so a pure-acquisition
        persona sees a layout item for a field they cannot read, which Lightning simply omits
        from render - the same protection every other dual-module field on this layout already
        relies on. A user holding BOTH an acquisition and a disposition permission set set will
        see them everywhere, which is an accepted, pre-existing class of residual on this shared
        layout, not something introduced by this change.

        Placement: Buyer__c sits with Opportunity__c at the top of column 1 (who this NDA
        concerns); Materials_Released_Date__c sits at the end of column 1, alongside the other
        NDA lifecycle dates (Date_Sent__c, Date_Signed__c).
    -->
    <!--
        REMOVED 2026-08-20: <excludeButtons>SmartFillEnrich</excludeButtons>. This line arrived
        via a RETRIEVE from usman-dpeg (commit b426598, "Retrieve Notes & Attachments onto the
        LOI, NDA and PSA Version layouts"), not hand-authored, and it blocked every subsequent
        deploy of this file with:
          "In field: excludeButtons, no such standard action: SmartFillEnrich"
        Verified safe to remove, not just to silence: SmartFillEnrich is not a QuickActionDefinition
        in this org, does not appear in NDA__c's sobject describe, and - the decisive check - is
        absent from the full standard-action inventory the UI API actions endpoint returns for a
        live NDA__c record (13 actions: NewEvent, NewTask, LogACall, NewCase, Edit, Delete, Clone,
        ChangeOwnerOne, ChangeRecordType, PrintableView, Share, RecordShareHierarchy, Submit,
        AssignRecordLabel - no SmartFillEnrich). excludeButtons only ever HIDES a button; excluding
        one that does not exist is a no-op, so deleting the exclusion changes nothing a user sees.
        🔴 A future retrieve of this layout from the same org will RE-INTRODUCE this line (the org
        emits the token on retrieve even though it rejects it on deploy - a platform asymmetry).
        Whoever hits that should re-apply this same removal rather than re-investigate from
        scratch.
    -->
    <layoutSections>
